@* Which seat this is: a numbered disc in the spirit's own colour, and the word for it. The
   recorded game's player card heads itself with one and so does the setup screen's seat dialog,
   and they had a copy each — same disc, same type, one of them free to drift.

   Untinted while the seat has no spirit yet, which only the setup screen can be: a coloured disc
   there would be claiming a choice that has not been made. *@

<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-medium text-ink-500">
    <span class="disc h-6 w-6 text-[11px] font-semibold"
          style="@DiscStyle">@Number</span>
    <span class="uppercase tracking-wide">Player @Number@(Total is { } total ? $" of {total}" : null)</span>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The seat's place at the table, counting from one.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Number { get; set; }

    /// <summary>How many seats there are, where the badge is worn by a dialog opened on one of
    /// them and "which of how many" is the thing being said. Omit on a card that sits among the
    /// others, where the count is there to be seen.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int? Total { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The spirit's colour. Null while the seat is still empty.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Color { get; set; }

    private string DiscStyle => Color is { } color
        ? $"background-color: {color}; color: white;"
        : "background-color: var(--color-ink-100); color: var(--color-ink-600);";
}
